  "query_preview": "..An upper low along the New Mexico/Colorado border will \ncontinue to push east today as shortwave ridging over California \nbegins to nose in from the west. The shortwave ridge axis will shift \nacross the state on Tuesday. A system will move to our north across \nthe Great Basin Tuesday night and Wednesday, flattening the ridge \nacross Arizona. Baggy troughiness will persist behind this system \nThursday and Friday. Stronger upper level ridging then takes place \nacross the desert southwest over the upcoming weekend.\n\nClearing skies continues to take place from west to east across \nsoutheast Arizona today behind the exiting low pressure system. High \ntemperatures today will top out 5-12 degrees below normal, with \nhighs generally in the upper 60s to lower 70s. The heavy rain this \nlast weekend led to significant rises on some of the mainstem \nrivers, creeks and washes across the forecast area, with a few areas \nstill having impacts. Please refer to the HYDROLOGY section below \nfor additional details. \n\nOtherwise, periods of high clouds this week and high temperatures \nTuesday through the upcoming weekend 3-8 degrees below normal.",
